 AIDS Relief. U.S. Five-year global HIV/AIDS strategy.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://2001-2009.state.gov/s/gac/plan/c11652.htm">http://2001-2009.state.gov/s/gac/plan/c11652.htm</ext-link>. Accessed 12 March 2009</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000059-Office2"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>Office of the US Global AIDS Coordinator</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>Report on work force capacity and HIV/AIDS.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.state.gov/documents/organization/69651.pdf">http://www.state.gov/documents/organization/69651.pdf</ext-link>. Accessed 12 March 2009</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000059-Buv1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buv&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalibala</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>McIntyre</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Stronger health systems for more effective HIV/AIDS prevention and care.</article-title><source>Int J Health Plann Manage</source><volume>18</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>S41</fpage><lpage>S51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14661940</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000059-U.S.1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>U.S. Agency for International Development</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Our work: A better future for all.</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.usaid.gov/our_work/">http://www.usaid.gov/our_work/</ext-link>. Accessed 12 March 2009</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000059-World6"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="other"><collab>World Health Organization</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Major health system constraints to improving HIV